WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.522 --> 00:00:08.117
Here is a simple booking journey: choose a service and time, enter your details, then see a clear confirmation.

2
00:00:11.008 --> 00:00:14.690
The visitor chooses an appointment type and an available slot.

3
00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:19.541
The unavailable time is disabled, making the next step clear.

4
00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:26.342
When the timezone changes, the selected time stays consistent.

5
00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:31.628
Ten in London becomes six in the evening in Hong Kong, with the timezone shown.

6
00:00:33.995 --> 00:00:40.897
The visitor adds their details, and the confirmation keeps the service, time and reference together.

7
00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:44.334
Going back also preserves the chosen slot.

8
00:00:46.123 --> 00:00:54.058
For your Acuity setup, I would review team availability and booking rules, then test confirmations and rescheduling.

